     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"From phishing:initialAccess alone, the attacker reaches only iotDevice:exploitPublicApp, mailClient:execution and tokenCache:credentialAccess. All four target parents are blocked. (1) codeRepo:collection needs hypervisor, printServer or backupHost. (2) shareMount:collection needs printServer. (3) dbReplica:collection needs jumpHost or secretsManager. (4) vaultRead:collection needs printServer, serviceAccount or secretsManager. Each of these depends on something unreachable. workstation:execution needs wifiGuest or supplychain, which blocks browserStore, apiToken, dbLogin, ssoLogin and configSecret via workstation. memoryDump:credentialAccess needs ciRunner (which needs vpnGateway) or supplychain, so rdpLogin fails and printServer fails. kerberoast needs wifiGuest or vpnGateway, so backupHost fails. dmzWeb needs vpnGateway or wifiGuest. So crownData:exfiltrate is not reachable.\"}"
    }
